            {
                "entry_id": "e066a12b-f17e-33f1-a512-affd8b8fbe70",
                "word": "dixie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ca76d6df-97f5-4fa7-b7bc-9b0f8bdff667",
                        "entry_id": "e066a12b-f17e-33f1-a512-affd8b8fbe70",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "dixies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c3cebb08-3d75-30ec-9e78-1c6b5d1dd4ed",
                        "entry_id": "e066a12b-f17e-33f1-a512-affd8b8fbe70",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A large iron pot, used in the army."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e8323d9-abd8-4710-afa3-48740c44bdfd",
                                "sense_id": "c3cebb08-3d75-30ec-9e78-1c6b5d1dd4ed",
                                "text": "four men generally like to mess together, and one cooking pot among them takes the place of a mess-tin or \"dixie\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "03d76595-42c5-4476-a806-8f945ee4d07f",
                                "sense_id": "c3cebb08-3d75-30ec-9e78-1c6b5d1dd4ed",
                                "text": "Then from the communication trenches came dixies or iron pots, filled with steaming tea, which had two wooden stakes through their handles, and were carried by two men."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "340a9b68-68cd-431f-af6f-269753d077be",
                                "sense_id": "c3cebb08-3d75-30ec-9e78-1c6b5d1dd4ed",
                                "text": "And what those ‘dixies’ of hot tea signified no one knows who wasn't there to wait for them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "43e973d8-ed19-4834-8315-846b934868fc",
                                "sense_id": "c3cebb08-3d75-30ec-9e78-1c6b5d1dd4ed",
                                "text": "Army rum is potent stuff, especially when the supplies of tea and water have run out, and one drinks it neat out of a dixie."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f4aecded-e65f-4d48-a558-ac58d1dd4baf",
                        "source_entry_id": "e066a12b-f17e-33f1-a512-affd8b8fbe70",
                        "source_sense_id": "c3cebb08-3d75-30ec-9e78-1c6b5d1dd4ed",
                        "source_sense_description": "a large iron pot, used in the army",
                        "target_lang_word": "котело́к",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "котело́к",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e5a0e93-bb87-34c2-81cd-c0a9c3ab6e4c",
                                        "entry_id": "1914e6d8-f068-3173-aa88-c01100a1929c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "уменьш. к котёл; походная посуда для приготовления пищи в виде небольшого котла"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aeafa26f-ffa0-4258-a29e-4537baeae827",
                                                "sense_id": "5e5a0e93-bb87-34c2-81cd-c0a9c3ab6e4c",
                                                "text": "А на печке кипит котелок, в нём варится суп."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7151aa8e-5b73-4f0f-9db2-6c090948b574",
                                                "sense_id": "5e5a0e93-bb87-34c2-81cd-c0a9c3ab6e4c",
                                                "text": "Бянкин молча подал Малешкину котелок с пшённой кашей, полбанки свиной тушенки, хлеб и фляжку с водкой."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea84759f-c974-3dfe-a8db-f866f637864c",
                                        "entry_id": "1914e6d8-f068-3173-aa88-c01100a1929c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "шляпа, по форме напоминаюшая котелок [1]"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c75a9bf8-35b4-404a-bc5c-9d54e720a551",
                                                "sense_id": "ea84759f-c974-3dfe-a8db-f866f637864c",
                                                "text": "Ему купили шляпу «панама», котелок, несколько галстуков и тоже ночные туфли."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09df1dc2-27fa-4372-b5fa-5ed8ddb57aab",
                                                "sense_id": "ea84759f-c974-3dfe-a8db-f866f637864c",
                                                "text": "Потом Генрих оделся в свой немецкий костюм и котелок на голову, в руках тросточка: они с Иваном Васильичем должны были устраивать Смолинского в больницу."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ac44111-be55-4d5d-a94e-5d2b4eb47815",
                                                "sense_id": "ea84759f-c974-3dfe-a8db-f866f637864c",
                                                "text": "Он снял с головы котелок и застенчиво приглаживал ладонью белесые волосы."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3016f8f-0a6d-3c26-8aca-5000ba3c0da7",
                                        "entry_id": "1914e6d8-f068-3173-aa88-c01100a1929c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "перен., шутл. то же, что голова"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74ca105d-9835-4f0c-8382-f1e286381869",
                                                "sense_id": "d3016f8f-0a6d-3c26-8aca-5000ba3c0da7",
                                                "text": "Если в голове каша, значит, котелок таки варит!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
